<title>USA: Fair weather continues for Brazil coffee - WSC.</title>
<headline>Fair weather continues for Brazil coffee - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Favorable conditions for Brazil's coffee trees and maturing crop are expected to continue, Weather Services Corp said in an update on Friday.</p>
<p>According to WSC, cooler-than-normal conditions are expected, but no damaging cold is indicated as there are no major cold air masses forecast for the area.</p>
<p>The weather this morning was mostly fair and temperatures ranged from the middle 40s to middle 50s F (7-13C).</p>
<p>Fair to partly cloudy skies are expected in the coffee belt during the next five to seven days, with low temperatures ranging from the 40s to low 50s (5-12 C).</p>
<p>WSC expects milder weather to arrive during the middle of next week.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity desk 212 859-1640))</p>
